    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nExcess 475,000\n\nSherry FitzGerald Radford are delighted to bring to the market this exceptional detached four-bedroom A-rated dormer bungalow, completed in 2024 and superbly positioned within a quiet residential cul-de-sac of just five detached homes.\n\nIdeally located on the Hook Peninsula, the property is within easy reach of the picturesque villages of Duncannon and Fethard-on-Sea, while the stunning Hook Peninsula coastline and Hook Lighthouse are also close by. Combining an enviable location with outstanding energy efficiency, generous accommodation and an exceptional standard of finish, this is a truly special home.\n\nThe property was built to an impressive standard, with the specification including an air-to-water heating system, double-glazed windows, a beautifully appointed Kitchen from \"Kitchen World\" with a comprehensive range of integrated appliances, stylish fully tiled bathrooms and a private septic tank.\n\nSince purchasing the property, the current owners have further enhanced the home with considerable thought and flair, creating a warm and individual interior that is both stylish and exceptionally comfortable. Features include beautiful Italian stone tiling throughout the Kitchen / Dining / Sunroom and Utility, striking Douglas Fir beams in the vaulted ceiling of the sun room and a wonderful south-west-facing patio which wraps around the rear of the property, creating an ideal setting for outdoor entertaining and enjoying the afternoon and evening sun.\n\nThe accommodation is particularly well laid out over two floors. On the ground floor, the welcoming entrance hall leads to a generous living room, dining room, beautifully appointed kitchen, sun room, utility room, two bedrooms, shower room and home office. Upstairs are two further impressive bedrooms, both benefiting from walk-in wardrobes, with one enjoying an ensuite, together with a separate family bathroom and store room.\n\nExternally, the property is equally impressive. The gardens have been newly landscaped and thoughtfully planted with an abundance of fruit trees, laurels and hedging. While the planting is still young, it has been carefully designed to mature beautifully and create a wonderful sense of privacy and seclusion around the house.\n\nThe south-west aspect is a particular highlight, with the landscaped gardens and wraparound patio providing an exceptional outdoor space for relaxing, entertaining or simply enjoying the peaceful surroundings.\n\nA detached garage further complements the property, providing excellent additional storage and featuring an up-and-over door.\n\nThis is a beautifully presented, energy-efficient modern home which combines quality construction with thoughtful upgrades, attractive landscaping and a superb location on the Hook Peninsula. Properties of this calibre and setting rarely come to the market and early viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 2.45m x 4.83m + 6.04m x 1.19m + 1.1m x 2.01m\nLaminate flooring\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.62m x 3.34m\nPicture window to front, laminate flooring\n\nLiving Room - 4.67m x 4.55m\nPicture windows to rear, feature multi fuel stove with wooden mantle and stone hearth, laminate flooring, recessed lighting\n\nDining Room - 4.36m x 3.29m\nStunning stone flooring, double doors to sun room, double doors to\n\nKitchen - 4.74m x 3.21m\nFitted wall and floor units, double sink, integrated dishwasher, built in oven, hob, extractor fan, built in fridge / freezer, butchers block tiled splashback, recessed lighting, stone tiled flooring\n\nPlant Room - 3.18m x 1.89m\nDoor to rear, stone tiled flooring, plumbed for washing machine, fitted floor storage unit, heating system with water tank\n\nSun Room - 5.15m x 4.09m\nTriple aspect room with laminate flooring, vaulted ceiling with feature \"Douglas Fir\" beams, double doors to rear\n\nStudy - 3.62m x 3.08m\nPicture window to front, laminate flooring\n\nShower Room - 2.39m x 1.56m\nFully tiled suite comprising step in shower with thermostate shower, wc, wash hand basin with storage, wall hung illuminated mirror, towel rail\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.44m x 2.94m\nPicture window to front, laminate flooring\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nLanding - 4.43m x 1.18m\nHatch to attic with stira staircase, storage cupboard (1.18m x 1.89m) shelved with laminate flooring\n\nBedroom 2 - 5.38m x 3.35m(max)\nPicture window to side, laminate flooring\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - 2.14m x 1.87m\nWalk in storage area with shelving and hangin space, laminate flooring\n\nBathroom - 2.55m x 2.01m\nFully tiled suite comprising bath with telephone shower attachment, wc, wash hand basin with storage, wall hung illuminated mirror, towel rail, velux window\n\nBedroom 1 - 6.18m x 5.38m\nPicture window to side, laminate flooring, winder eave storage\n\nWalk in wardrobe - \nDivided into shelved area (3.51m x 1.89m) opening into hanging space area (2.28m x 1.27m with laminate flooring\n\nEnsuite - 2.25m x 2.02m\nFully tiled suite comprising step in shower unit with termostate shower, wc, wash hand basin with storage, wall hung illuminated mirror, towel rail, velux window\n\n"
